## Why This Is Asked
Tests ability to design a robust online ICA system for automotive cabins with real-time constraints and hardware faults.

## Key Concepts
- Online convolutive ICA with dynamic model order
- Robust whitening under missing sensors
- Dropout-aware demixer reinitialization
- Cross-bin permutation continuity across time
- Edge-device latency and evaluation strategies

## Code Example
```javascript
// Pseudo: online ICA loop with dropout handling
while (streaming) {
  const frame = readFrame();
  const N = estimateSourceCount(frame);
  whiten(frame, N);
  if (dropoutDetected()) adjustDemixer(N);
  updateDemixer(N);
  alignPermutations(N);
}
```

## Follow-up Questions
- How would you validate with synthetic vs real data when ground truth is unavailable?
- Which metrics best reflect real-time separation quality under dropout conditions?

## Why This Is Asked
Semi-supervised ICA in a mobile, real-world setting tests robustness to nonstationary channels and practical ambiguities that pure unsupervised methods struggle with. The calibration window anchors global alignment without sacrificing online adaptability.

## Key Concepts
- Semi-supervised ICA to resolve permutation/sign drift across bins
- Online whitening with forgetting factor in a convolutive model
- Adaptive selection between per-bin ICA and joint diagonalization
- Gain-drift compensation and robustification to wind/noise
- Ground-truth based evaluation (SDR/SIR) and lightweight diarization cues

## Code Example
```javascript
// Pseudo: anchorPermutation using calibration data
function anchorPermutation(calibStim, demixMatrix) {
  // compute permutation that best aligns calibStim with known sources
  // returns adjusted demixMatrix
  const perm = computeBestPermutation(calibStim, sourcesKnown);
  return applyPermutation(demixMatrix, perm);
}
```

